  "sn11.5:0.3": "<p>See also: <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn21'>DN 21</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn1.71'>SN 1:71</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn7.2'>SN 7:2</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn35.248'>SN 35:207</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an7.64'>AN 7:60</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dhp129-145#dhp129'>Dhp 129–134</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/snp3.3'>Sn 3:3</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/snp4.15'>Sn 4:15</a></p>",
  "sn11.5:1.1": "",
  "sn11.5:1.2": "The devas &amp; asuras were two groups of deities who fought for control of heaven (like the gods &amp; titans in Greek mythology). The devas eventually won. The asuras, known for their fierce anger, later became classed as angry demons and, in some Buddhist cosmologies, are regarded as a class of being lower than human.",
